# Target C-II — sharpen the smallest-leaf center fan to `>0.7404D`

**Date:** 2026-09-15  
**Status:** proof-only phase-resolved structural strengthening  
**Scope:** full-core Type-II branch with `t=(q-k)/D<=1.844`  
**Dependencies:** `target_c_small_leaf_center_fan_073_t1844_2026-09-15.md` and its exact upstream constants  
**LEVEL I STATUS:** `STILL OPEN. C-II REMAINS OPEN.`

The existing small-leaf fan theorem proves a weighted average center-crossing degree
larger than `0.73D`. Its finite optimization has substantially more room. Keeping the
same upstream constants and rerunning only the final two endpoint inequalities gives

\[
\boxed{
{E(C,Q_V)\over P_VD}>0.7404D-o(D),
}
\tag{F7404.1}

where `Q_V` is the retained weighted outer-to-outer pair family in the smallest leaf
phase of the dominant exact `pi/3` orbit and `P_VD` is its total retained pair weight.
Consequently some positive-weight smallest-leaf outer-to-outer train is crossed by

\[
\boxed{>0.7404D-o(D)}
\tag{F7404.2}

center-phase complete trains.

This note does not change the argument or its scope. It only replaces the rounded
threshold `L=0.73` by the rigorously certified `L=0.7404`.

---

## 1. Reuse the exact parent reduction

The parent theorem established, uniformly for `t<=1.844`, the safe constants

\[
W_0=1.915963,
\qquad
E_0=0.9068958,
\qquad
C>0.8538,
\qquad
z_V>0.616.
\tag{F7404.3}

It also proved

\[
V>0.308-o(1),
\qquad
P_V>0.616-V-o(1),
\tag{F7404.4}

and reduced the weighted average center degree to

\[
{E(C,Q_V)\over P_VD^2}
\ge
R(C,V)-o(1),
\tag{F7404.5}

with

\[
R(C,V)
=C-{C H(C)\over(2C+V-W_0)(0.616-V)},
\qquad
H(C)=C(W_0-C)-E_0.
\tag{F7404.6}

The feasible domain is

\[
0.8538<C<1.063,
\qquad
0.308<V\le {W_0-C\over2}.
\tag{F7404.7}

For fixed `C`, the `V` denominator

\[
(2C+V-W_0)(0.616-V)
\]

is concave. Hence the minimum of `R(C,V)` occurs at one of the same two endpoints:

\[
V=0.308,
\qquad
V={W_0-C\over2}.
\tag{F7404.8}

Nothing upstream depends on the old choice `L=0.73`.

---

## 2. Low-leaf endpoint at `L=0.7404`

Put

\[
L={7404\over10000}=0.7404.
\]

At `V=0.308`, the condition `R(C,V)>L` is equivalent to

\[
N_{lo,L}(C)>0,
\]

where

\[
N_{lo,L}(C)
=(C-L)(2C+0.308-W_0)(0.308)
-C[C(W_0-C)-E_0].
\tag{F7404.9}

The exact `Fraction` certificate proves that `N_{lo,L}` is strictly convex throughout
the feasible `C` interval. Its unique critical point lies in

\[
0.88341<C_*<0.88342,
\]

and a derivative-Lipschitz enclosure gives

\[
\boxed{
N_{lo,L}(C)>0.00233998
}
\tag{F7404.10}

at the minimum.

---

## 3. Balanced-leaf endpoint at `L=0.7404`

At

\[
V={W_0-C\over2},
\]

the condition `R(C,V)>L` is equivalent to

\[
N_{hi,L}(C)>0,
\]

where

\[
N_{hi,L}(C)
=(C-L){3C-W_0\over2}
\left(0.616-{W_0-C\over2}\right)
-C[C(W_0-C)-E_0].
\tag{F7404.11}

Again the exact certificate proves strict convexity. The unique critical point is
bracketed by

\[
0.90484<C_*<0.90485,
\]

and the exact minimum enclosure is

\[
\boxed{
N_{hi,L}(C)>4.47\times10^{-6}>0.
}
\tag{F7404.12}

This endpoint controls the sharpening. Its margin is small compared with the old
`0.73` certificate but remains exact and positive.

Equations (F7404.10)--(F7404.12) imply

\[
R(C,V)>0.7404
\]

throughout the full parent domain, proving (F7404.1).

---

## 4. From weighted average to one actual train

Write the retained smallest-leaf outer-to-outer family as positive weights `w_tau`
and let `d_tauD` be the number of center-phase complete trains crossing `tau`. Then

\[
{E(C,Q_V)\over P_VD}
={\sum_\tau w_\tau d_\tauD\over\sum_\tau w_\tau}.
\tag{F7404.13}

If every positive-weight train had `d_tau<=0.7404+o(1)`, the weighted average would
satisfy the same upper bound, contradicting (F7404.1). Hence at least one retained
outer-to-outer train has (F7404.2).

This is the same weighted-average inference as in the audited `0.73` theorem; no
unweighted density floor is inferred.

---

## 5. Exact certificate and numerical frontier

Run

`python3 research/verify_target_c_small_leaf_center_fan_7404_t1844_2026-09-15.py`.

It uses only exact rational arithmetic for the finite optimization. The controlling
balanced endpoint has certified polynomial margin greater than `4e-6`.

Numerical minimization of the already-reduced endpoint formula places the rounded
frontier near

\[
0.74050\ldots,
\]

but this note claims only `0.7404`. No numerical sign is load-bearing.

---

## 6. Downstream effect

The corrected dual-tree rectangle extraction uses only three fan inputs:

1. retained pair weight `P_V>0.0848-o(1)`;
2. weighted average center degree;
3. the center-phase size ceiling `C<1.063+o(1)`.

Replacing `0.73` by `0.7404` therefore strengthens every subsequent good-leaf,
backbone, and complete-rectangle constant without changing topology. Optimizing those
thresholds is the next immediate propagation step.

**Disposition:** exact proof-only fan strengthening. C-II and Level I remain open.
